# Gurudevi Web Environment Configuration
#
# === For Team Members (With Doppler Access) ===
# Real secrets are stored in Doppler: https://dashboard.doppler.com → gurudevi-mobile project
# For local dev: Use `doppler run -- <your-command>` to inject secrets
# Do not download secrets to `.env` during normal development; use `doppler run`
# Get started: https://docs.doppler.com/docs/cli
#
# Run with Doppler:
#   doppler run -- pnpm --filter gurudevi-web dev
#
# === For Contributors (Without Doppler Access) ===
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the required values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#   # Edit .env.local and fill in your values
#   pnpm --filter gurudevi-web dev
#
# For local Supabase (optional, for DB work):
#   supabase start
#   # Copy API URL + publishable key from supabase status into .env.local
#
# See: docs/decisions/2026-08-25-transparent-hosted-oss.md
#
# === Environment Variables ===
# The values below are placeholders for reference only
# Required vars are marked in comments

# Supabase Configuration (REQUIRED for Sanctuary Account Surface; Not required for Explore Showroom)
# Get these from your Supabase project settings > API
# For local dev: use http://127.0.0.1:54321 + key from `supabase start`
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Sanctuary API Endpoint (Optional: defaults to mock/local fallback if unset)
VITE_API_URL=

# Support Form Endpoint (Optional)
VITE_SUPPORT_FORM_ACTION=

# Optional: Fallback from Expo env vars (if sharing the same Doppler mobile dev config)
# vite.config.ts will automatically fall back to EXPO_PUBLIC_* if VITE_* is not set:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
